# Tests avec PHPUnit dans Lunar Quanta

Lunar Quanta est livré avec plus de 1200 tests. Découvrez comment tester votre propre code.

## Configuration

### phpunit.xml

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit bootstrap="vendor/autoload.php" colors="true">
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="Unit">
            <directory>tests/Unit</directory>
        </testsuite>
        <testsuite name="Integration">
            <directory>tests/Integration</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <coverage>
        <include>
            <directory suffix=".php">src</directory>
        </include>
    </coverage>
</phpunit>
```

### Lancer les Tests

```bash
# Tous les tests
./vendor/bin/phpunit

# Avec descriptions
./vendor/bin/phpunit --testdox

# Un fichier spécifique
./vendor/bin/phpunit tests/Service/PostServiceTest.php

# Un test spécifique
./vendor/bin/phpunit --filter testCreatePost
```

## Tests Unitaires

### Structure de Base

```php
<?php

namespace Tests\Unit\Service;

use PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase;
use App\Service\Calculator;

class CalculatorTest extends TestCase
{
    private Calculator $calculator;

    protected function setUp(): void
    {
        $this->calculator = new Calculator();
    }

    public function testAddition(): void
    {
        $result = $this->calculator->add(2, 3);

        $this->assertEquals(5, $result);
    }

    public function testDivisionByZeroThrowsException(): void
    {
        $this->expectException(\DivisionByZeroError::class);

        $this->calculator->divide(10, 0);
    }
}
```

### Data Providers

```php
/**
 * @dataProvider additionProvider
 */
public function testAdditionWithProvider(int $a, int $b, int $expected): void
{
    $this->assertEquals($expected, $this->calculator->add($a, $b));
}

public static function additionProvider(): array
{
    return [
        'positifs' => [1, 2, 3],
        'négatifs' => [-1, -2, -3],
        'mixte' => [-1, 3, 2],
        'zéros' => [0, 0, 0],
    ];
}
```

## Mocking

### Mock Simple

```php
public function testSendEmailCallsMailer(): void
{
    $mailer = $this->createMock(MailerInterface::class);

    $mailer->expects($this->once())
           ->method('send')
           ->with(
               $this->equalTo('user@example.com'),
               $this->stringContains('Bienvenue')
           );

    $service = new NotificationService($mailer);
    $service->sendWelcomeEmail('user@example.com');
}
```

### Mock avec Retour

```php
public function testGetUserReturnsUser(): void
{
    $repository = $this->createMock(UserRepository::class);

    $repository->method('find')
               ->with(1)
               ->willReturn(new User(1, 'John'));

    $service = new UserService($repository);
    $user = $service->getUser(1);

    $this->assertEquals('John', $user->getName());
}
```

### Spy (vérifier les appels)

```php
public function testLogsOnError(): void
{
    $logger = $this->createMock(LoggerInterface::class);

    $logger->expects($this->once())
           ->method('error')
           ->with($this->stringContains('Failed'));

    $service = new PaymentService($logger);
    $service->process(invalidData: true);
}
```

## Tests d'Intégration

### Avec Base de Données

```php
class PostServiceIntegrationTest extends TestCase
{
    private PostService $service;
    private string $testDir;

    protected function setUp(): void
    {
        $this->testDir = sys_get_temp_dir() . '/test_posts_' . uniqid();
        mkdir($this->testDir);

        $storage = new FileStorage($this->testDir);
        $this->service = new PostService($storage);
    }

    protected function tearDown(): void
    {
        // Nettoyer
        array_map('unlink', glob($this->testDir . '/*'));
        rmdir($this->testDir);
    }

    public function testCreateAndRetrievePost(): void
    {
        $post = new Post('Mon Article', 'Contenu...');
        $this->service->save($post);

        $retrieved = $this->service->find($post->getId());

        $this->assertEquals('Mon Article', $retrieved->getTitle());
    }
}
```

## Tests de Contrôleurs

```php
class UserControllerTest extends TestCase
{
    public function testIndexReturnsUsers(): void
    {
        $userService = $this->createMock(UserService::class);
        $userService->method('all')->willReturn([
            new User(1, 'John'),
            new User(2, 'Jane'),
        ]);

        $controller = new UserController($userService);
        $response = $controller->index();

        $this->assertEquals(200, $response->getStatusCode());
        $this->assertJson($response->getContent());

        $data = json_decode($response->getContent(), true);
        $this->assertCount(2, $data);
    }
}
```

## Assertions Utiles

```php
// Égalité
$this->assertEquals($expected, $actual);
$this->assertSame($expected, $actual); // Type strict

// Booléens
$this->assertTrue($value);
$this->assertFalse($value);
$this->assertNull($value);

// Chaînes
$this->assertStringContainsString('foo', $string);
$this->assertMatchesRegularExpression('/pattern/', $string);

// Tableaux
$this->assertCount(3, $array);
$this->assertContains($item, $array);
$this->assertArrayHasKey('key', $array);

// Objets
$this->assertInstanceOf(User::class, $object);

// Exceptions
$this->expectException(InvalidArgumentException::class);
$this->expectExceptionMessage('Invalid input');
```

## Couverture de Code

```bash
# Générer le rapport HTML
./vendor/bin/phpunit --coverage-html coverage/

# Voir le pourcentage
./vendor/bin/phpunit --coverage-text
```

## Bonnes Pratiques

1. **Un test = une assertion** (idéalement)
2. **Nommage explicite** : `testUserCannotLoginWithInvalidPassword`
3. **Arrange-Act-Assert** : séparer les 3 phases
4. **Isolation** : chaque test indépendant
5. **Fast** : tests rapides = plus de runs

## Conclusion

Les tests de Lunar Quanta garantissent :

- **Fiabilité** : 1200+ tests
- **Confiance** : refactoring serein
- **Documentation** : les tests montrent l'usage
- **Qualité** : bugs détectés tôt

Testez, testez, testez !
